{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pegs are put in a board <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit apart both horizontally and vertically. A rubber band is stretched over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pegs as shown in the figure, forming a quadrilateral. Its area in square units is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f53bd3f40ff47916b824996e6c0b7cfa5d93c17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] int i,j; for(i=0; i&lt;5; i=i+1) { for(j=0; j&lt;4; j=j+1) { dot((i,j)); }} draw((0,1)--(1,3)--(4,1)--(3,0)--cycle, linewidth(0.7));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d14bc360ce38e6c8d548d3e29544c20dc541acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }4.5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 5.5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"370\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3df6ca185b3b9d326b6265dd0d26ae0a7ce655.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] int i,j; for(i=0; i&lt;5; i=i+1) { for(j=0; j&lt;4; j=j+1) { dot((i,j)); }} draw((0,1)--(1,3)--(4,1)--(3,0)--cycle, linewidth(0.7)); draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,3)--(0,3)--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,3),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(4,3),NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(4,0),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(1,3),N); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(4,1),E); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(3,0),S); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,(0,1),W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"195\" />\nWe draw in the rectangle bounding the given quadrilateral and label the points as shown. The area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/c/8acb7505e8e4cc5bf25623bc9160ca4e739eb4f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)(4) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />, while the areas of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2cecf090af263a60467ac6a2353b7c6d14be9d3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEH$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea90e6937e1190a3bcca66ef907234b61b3fac6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EBF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3140b72a608bd0c8079ea1631f94924228ee81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FCG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f8e1d64db5df60137d5a53a5e8018887879fffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GDH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> are, respectively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34e96b9e37da7219ddce5c9bf69487985f0265ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\text{area of } \\triangle AEH = \\frac{1}{2}(1)(2) = 1, \\\\ &amp;\\text{area of } \\triangle EBF = \\frac{1}{2}(3)(2) = 3, \\\\ &amp;\\text{area of } \\triangle FCG = \\frac{1}{2}(1)(1) = \\frac{1}{2}, \\text{ and} \\\\ &amp;\\text{area of } \\triangle GDH = \\frac{1}{2}(3)(1) = \\frac{3}{2}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"274\" height=\"166\" />\nHence the area of the given quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7da80d3e1f4e55ab8bf24afdfb67666c20bee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-\\left(1+3+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\right) = \\boxed{\\text{(E)} \\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"254\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of lattice points (i.e. pegs on the board) strictly inside the quadrilateral is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the number of lattice points on its boundary is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pick%27s_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pick&#39;s theorem\">Pick's theorem</a>, its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/5/c75f669f3cd8fa846d5f1b38971c60a242d9edca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+\\frac{4}{2}-1 = \\boxed{\\text{(E)} \\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174749\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.094 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 157/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3933/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.263      1 -total\n 57.71%    7.654      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.27%    5.208      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10296:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174749 and revision id 217117. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}